hgc@163.com\n招标代理机构：中信国际招标有限公司\n联 系 人：郭女士 、张先生\n监督部门：郑州市水利工程招标投标管理办公室\n地址：郑州市颍河路110号\n电话：0371- 67721936\n传真：0371- 67721936\n\n\n========\n搜索关键词：郑州金水河灾后重建 防洪标准 投资规模\n\n网页标题：我市将实施金水河综合整治工程 - 郑州市发展和改革委员会\n\n网页链接：https://fgw.zhengzhou.gov.cn/xmjs/6257247.jhtml\n\n发布时间：2022-02-07T10:49:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：我市将实施金水河综合整治工程\n来源：市发展改革委 时间：2022-02-07 10:49\n2022年1月30日，郑州市发改委批复金水河综合整治工程初步设计。工程南起郭家咀水库坝下、北至东风渠，治理河道总长约22.3公里，红线范围内总面积约213.1公顷，主要包括河道安全保障、桥梁恢复提升、水质保障与生态提升、绿化完善、智慧管理等工程，概算投资253369万元。\n该项目是“720”特大暴雨灾害灾后重建工程，对提升金水河整体防洪排涝能力保证我市城区安全意义重大。工程建设将打通金水河河道阻水点，增加河道行洪排涝能力，做好雨污水分流，保障行洪安全，统筹做好公共空间整治，实现河安、路通、水清、岸美，将金水河打造成为造福郑州人民的幸福河。\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：郑州金水河灾后重建 防洪标准 投资规模\n\n网页标题：金水河综合整治工程[综合工程]_百科\n\n网页链接：https://m.baike.com/wiki/%E9%87%91%E6%B0%B4%E6%B2%B3%E7%BB%BC%E5%90%88%E6%95%B4%E6%B2%BB%E5%B7%A5%E7%A8%8B/7581649385143566371\n\n网页内容：金水河综合整治工程[综合工程]_百科\n金水河综合整治工程是河南省郑州市于2021年正式启动的一项重大城市基础设施与生态修复项目。该工程主要为了解决金水河长期存在的行洪排涝能力不足、服务设施陈旧、河道生态功能缺失等问题。\n建设历程\n工程的前期研究工作于2020年6月启动。2021年7月，项目取得立项批复，并于同年11月下旬正式开工建设先行示范段。2023年1月，工程实现全线开工建设。工程主体已于2023年底具备行洪条件。\n工程规划\n金水河综合整治工程治理范围从上游的郭家咀水库起，至下游的东风渠止，治理河道总长约22.3公里。工程被定位为河南省灾后恢复重建的标志性项目之一，其根本目标是恢复和提升河道的基础功能。通过综合整治，将金水河的防洪标准从原有的5至50年一遇，全面提升至100年一遇，并结合上游水库与分洪工程。除了防洪，工程还致力于构建连续贯通的滨水慢行系统，完善便民服务设施，并提升河道的水生态与水环境。\n设计理念\n工程设计秉持“一脉、四水、五区”的总体规划理念。其中，“五区”是指根据河道流经区域的自然与城市特征，从上游到下游将全线划分为五个主题鲜明的片区:生态郊野区(郭家咀水库-南水北调干渠)、活力运动区(南水北调干渠-嵩山南路)、智慧创享区(嵩山南路-北闸口铁路桥)、市井人文区(北闸口铁路桥-未来路)以及都市水岸区(未来路-东风渠)。\n整治内容\n水安全保障:这是工程的核心，主要通过河道扩挖、卡口段拓宽、岸坡防护、新建拦河闸与分洪闸等措施。\n水生态修复:采取控源截污(如污水主干管外迁)、生态补水、恢复水生植物等举措。\n滨水服务提升:增设亲水平台、过水汀步，贯通两岸慢行步道，并配套建设驿站、儿童及健身活动场地等便民设施。\n沿河路与桥梁改造:对沿河道路进行综合整治，并改造提升阻水桥梁，新建人行桥。\n工程投资\n工程批复概算投资为34.02亿元，主要包括两部分:一是河道综合整治25.33亿元，全长22公里，建设内容为河道防洪排涝能力提升、污水主干管外迁及雨水口改造、亲水步道贯通、阻水桥梁改造提升、新建人行桥、便民服务设施完善、生态景观及河道管理服务水平提升等。河道综合整治部分施工费20.33亿元，其他费用共5亿元(主要用于勘察、设计、监理、评估、监测、管线迁改、工程预备费等)。采用最低价中标方式进行招标，中标价为13.85亿元，其中，综合整治共20.12公里、共9.97亿元，折合每公里造价约4950万元;调洪及分洪闸部分长2.18公里、共3.88亿元。二是沿河路及涉铁节点改造8.69亿元，建设内容为沿河路拆除外迁新建道路，下穿铁路隧道2处，下穿铁路污水干管2处，雨水泵站1座，人行天桥2座以及下穿铁路段河道拓宽等，按有关要求由中国铁路郑州局集团有限公司负责代建。部分挂贴花岗岩石材的河道长度约10.8公里，面积约2.68万平方米，总造价约650万元，占总投资的0.2%，挂贴石材位于人行步道外侧。\n相关事件\n2024年7月7日至8日，郑州市出现区域性大暴雨，是今年入汛以来最强的一次降雨过程。根据郑州国家气象站监测数据，8日00时至8日19时，降雨总量达到145.2毫米。金水河出现护坡坍塌、步道受损的情况，经核实，坍塌护坡位于金水河紫荆山路交叉口东南侧，为原有河堤，2019年地铁站建成后恢复。因该处属于地铁保护区域，根据有关规定，为保护地铁结构安全，避免施工扰动影响，该处护坡未纳入金水河综合整治工程范围，仅在原河道坡底设置3.0米宽亲水步道，结构形式为混凝土结构，未扰动原有边坡及河床结构。\n参考资料\n系统科学治理，提升行洪能力——郑州启动金水河综合整治\n关于打造郑州南区后海建议提案的答复\n郑州通报金水河综合整治工程情况 工程内容及目前进度公开\n关于金水河综合整治工程情况通报\n针对网传“郑州花34亿给河道干挂大理石砖”，官方最新通报\n关于金水河综合整治工程情况通报\n郑州通报\"河道贴砖\"\n因大暴雨金水河护坡坍塌、步道受损，郑州发布情况说明\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：郑州金水河灾后重建 防洪标准 投资规模\n\n网页标题：Untitled\n\n网页链接：https://public.zhengzhou.gov.cn/attachment/%E9%87%91%E6%B0%B4%E6%B2%B3%E7%BB%BC%E5%90%88%E6%95%B4%E6%B2%BB%E5%B7%A5%E7%A8%8B%E7%8E%AF%E8%AF%84%E6%8A%A5%E5%91%8A.pdf?lxkYtmdsazsQyGTyx0J1G6HF3bqVMdKBQxwndYcb2KV-qeXYYTax4ENmXxI4cMIQpL09mqcWUSjVtptpo8LuK7HzLXl_EQ==\n\n网页内容：2\n第二章项目概况...35\n2.1 工程概况...35\n2.2 工程现状...35\n2.2.1 河道现状...35\n2.2.2 排水口现状...36\n2.2.3 提防现状...36\n2.2.4 桥梁现状...37\n2.2.5 存在的问题...40\n2.3 项目建设必要性及建设任务...42\n2.3.1 建设必要性...42\n2.3.2 项目建设任务...43\n2.4 项目建设内容...43\n2.4.1 水安全保障工程...44\n2.4.2 沿河路综合整治提升工程...46\n2.4.3 桥梁恢复提升工程...46\n2.4.4 水质保障与生态提升工程...49\n2.4.5 绿化完善工程...68\n2.4.6 智慧管理工程...69\n2.4.7 工程等级及防洪标准...76\n2.4.8 建筑物级别...98\n2.4.9 河道蓝线及河道中心线布置...98\n2.4.10 河道纵､横断面布置...100\n2.4.11 河底比降...108\n2.4.12 河道水面线推算... 111\n2.4.13 项目与重大工程的衔接...113\n2.4.14 土料填筑...122\n2.4.15 河道规划水源...122\n2.5 施工组织设计...123\n2.5.1 施工导流...123\n2.5.2 主体施工工艺...124\n2.5.3 场外施工交通...131\n5\n6.1 施工期环境保护措施......\n设其他费为37930.64 万元;第三部分预备费为26931.57 万元;水土保持专项工\n程费1312.96 万元;环境保护专项工程费634.91 万元｡不含金水河穿越铁路段沿\n河路综合整治提升工程､智慧水务工程｡\n金水路燕庄水面节点改造工程(西起东明路西400 米处中州宾馆附近,东至\n金水路下游120m 现状拦水坝处,全长约0.75km)､金水路大石桥节点景观改造\n工程(西起金水路南阳路交叉口,东至河南出入境检疫检验局西围墙处｡全长约\n553m｡)､以及金水河跨铁路桥段(起点接现状建设路辅道,沿金水河东岸布\n设终点至铭功路｡道路全长1283.321m)单独立项实施,不在本次工程实施范围\n内｡\n2､项目特点\n①工程任务\n金水河目前主要承担着防洪排涝的功能,因两岸高差较大,沿岸园路不亲水\n不贯通;沿线大型公园均各自独立与河道缺乏联系,通达性不畅｡且沿线居住密\n度较高,百姓亲水､活动需求强烈,但现有场所均集中在河道的两侧,沿河道无\n停留空间,近水不亲水,空间割裂明显,公共空间缺乏｡为了解除汛期洪水对两\n4\n图1 评价工程程序\n4､关注的主要环境问题\n根据项目特点及所处区域的环境特征,关注的主要环境问题表现在:\n①施工期:施工扬尘对周围大气环境的影响;施工生产废水及施工人员生活\n污水对周围水体的影响;施工噪声对周围敏感点的影响;施工废弃物对环境的影\n第 二 阶 段\n依据相关规定确定环境影响评价文件类型\n1 研究相关技术文件和其他有关文件 2 进行初步工程分析 3 开展初步的环境现状调查\n1 环境影响识别和评价因子筛选\n2 明确评价重点和环境保护目标\n3 确定工作等级､评价范围和评价标准\n制定工作方案\n环境现状调查 监测与评价\n水河中上游,在分水口至郭家咀水库段依然缺少补水水源｡\n本次补水泵站规模按照0.8m3/s 设计,泵站扬程35m,装机功\n率528kW｡泵站采用钢筋混凝土沉井泵站,配套建设变配电间一 栋,管理用房一栋｡泵站选址位于金海路与金水河交叉口东南侧, 总占地面积2274.3 m2,其中综合管理用房292.5 m2,配电间75 m2, 泵站173.24 m2｡\n原位强 化净化\n工程\n为稳定金水河水质,控制藻类的繁殖和爆发,拟在帝湖内布\n局原位强化净化措施,包含湖岸布设固定生物循环床(FBR 滨岸 湿地)5200m2,湖底及湖岸种植水生植物41200m2,投放鱼类､蚌 类和螺类共8000kg,由此形成稳定的水生态系统,稳定和提升帝 湖出水水体的营养元素和透明度指标\n11\n水生态 系统修 复工程\n本工程结合河道本底､两岸特征及生物需求,从生物恢复和\n生境营造2 大方面入手,通过水生植物群落补植､鸟类生态岛与 辫状水系打造以及深潭工程与石块群工程等措施,整体提升金水 河河流生态系统健康程度,建设“有河有水､有鱼有草､人水和谐” 的生态河道｡工程规模方面,在郊野段营造鸟类生境13359m2,城 区段沿河挺水植被带8611 m2,共设置5 组平均深度1m 的深潭共 约2816 m2｡\n公园封 闭水体 活水工\n程\n本次根据公园内水体体积,考虑换水周期为30 天,从金水河\n提水进入公园水系,实现公园水体的活水｡\n人民公园设提水泵站一座,规模122m3/h,紫荆山公园设提水\n泵站一座,规模79m3/h｡\n郑州大学区块的花林碧波景观节点,现状分布有一水岸公园,\n本次根据公园内水体体积,综合考虑该水体自净能力,确定换水 周期为14 天,从金水河提水进入公园水系,实现公园水体的活水｡ 花林碧波景观节点设提水泵站一座,规模50m3/h｡\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：郑州金水河灾后重建 防洪标准 投资规模\n\n网页标题：关于金水河综合整治工程情况通报 - 郑州市城乡建设局\n\n网页链接：https://zzjsj.zhengzhou.gov.cn/tzgg/7620049.jhtml\n\n发布时间：2023-07-10T10:31:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：关于金水河综合整治工程情况通报\n来源：本站 时间：2023-07-10 10:31:35\n金水河是贯穿郑州主城区的一条城市河流。金水河综合整治工程前期研究工作于2020年6月启动，主要是为了解决金水河行洪排涝能力不足、服务设施陈旧、河道生态功能及服务功能缺失等问题，是集行洪排涝、生态功能修复和滨水服务百姓生活于一体的一项综合工程。\n\n![](https://zzjsj.zhengzhou.gov.cn/u/cms/jsj/202307/081810023cmn.png)\n图为河道整治断面示意\n工程内容及目前进度\n该工程2021年7月19日取得工程立项批复，2023年1月实现全线开工建设。工程批复概算投资为34.02亿元，主要包括两部分：一是河道综合整治25.33亿元，全长22公里，建设内容为河道防洪排涝能力提升、污水主干管外迁及雨水口改造、亲水步道贯通、阻水桥梁改造提升、新建人行桥、便民服务设施完善、生态景观及河道管理服务水平提升等。河道综合整治部分施工费20.33亿元，其他费用共5亿元（主要用于勘察、设计、监理、评估、监测、管线迁改、工程预备费等）。采用最低价中标方式进行招标，中标价为13.85亿元，其中，综合整治共20.12公里、共9.97亿元，折合每公里造价约4950万元；调洪及分洪闸部分长2.18公里、共3.88亿元。二是沿河路及涉铁节点改造8.69亿元，建设内容为沿河路拆除外迁新建道路，下穿铁路隧道2处，下穿铁路污水干管2处，雨水泵站1座，人行天桥2座以及下穿铁路段河道拓宽等，按有关要求由中国铁路郑州局集团有限公司负责代建。\n该工程部分挂贴花岗岩石材的河道长度约10.8公里，面积约2.68万平方米，总造价约650万元，占总投资的0.2%，挂贴石材位于人行步道外侧。目前，河道内主体工程和污水管道外迁等已完工，具备行洪条件，整体工程预计今年年底完工（涉铁路节点除外）。\n工程设计及“干挂石材”情况\n金水河综合整治工程设计采取公开招标方式，邀请国内一流水利工程设计公司参与竞标，经严格评审，最终由中国电建集团华东勘测设计研究院中标。在设计中，综合考虑金水河综合整治涉及护岸、堰坝、水闸及清淤清障等多个方面，基于河两岸路网密集、临河建筑物众多、以及柳树和法桐等高大乔木密布等实际情况，如果直接开挖拓宽，对环境影响较大，故采取H型护岸桩挡墙方案。该方案能够尽可能利用河道两岸的既有绿色植被，同时有效降低投资，结构安全性也能够满足规范要求。\n因护岸桩挡墙为H型预制构件，完成后接缝处不可避免存在不平整粗糙面，汛期对行洪有一定程度的影响，非汛期对行人也存在一定的安全风险，且裸露的护岸桩或挡墙观感较差，根据国内类似工程经验，对表面进行处理是必要的。目前，国内采用的通用处理方式主要有石材挂贴、石材湿贴、混凝土预制板材挂贴等。根据测算，单位面积投资中，混凝土预制板材挂贴单价过高，石材挂贴和湿贴投资相当，但石材湿贴易脱落、影响安全，经技术经济比较，选用石材挂贴工艺。具体施工中，所用石材为花岗岩，而非大理石，采用的是“先挂石材、后灌浆”的挂贴施工工艺，而非一般建筑立面采用的“干挂石材”施工工艺，具有较好耐久性、安全性。经计算，金水河若遇100年一遇洪水，其洪水流速在2—3米每秒，挂贴花岗岩立面可抵抗该流速的冲刷。\n\n![](https://zzjsj.zhengzhou.gov.cn/u/cms/jsj/202307/08175959u2y6.png)\n图为帝湖段整治后的实景\n\n![](https://zzjsj.zhengzhou.gov.cn/u/cms/jsj/202307/08180010a7i0.png)\n图为石材挂贴灌砂浆施工\n\n![](https://zzjsj.zhengzhou.gov.cn/u/cms/jsj/202307/09183603yuoz.png)\n![](https://zzjsj.zhengzhou.gov.cn/u/cms/jsj/202307/08180027fmjc.png)\n图为国内其他城市相同案例\n金水河综合整治工程完成之后，防洪方面结合上游郭家咀水库、调洪及分洪工程，将使防洪标准由5—50年一遇提升到100年一遇。同时，配套建设的驿站（含公厕）、节点广场、儿童活动场地、健身运动场地等，将完善服务功能，提升人居环境，便利市民休闲游憩。\n\n![](https://zzjsj.zhengzhou.gov.cn/u/cms/jsj/202307/09181714xzbh.png)\n图为帝湖段实景\n金水河综合整治关乎每一位郑州市民的切身利益，欢迎社会各界和广大人民群众的监督与建议，共同努力打造属于全体郑州市民的幸福河！\n郑州市金水河综合整治工程指挥部\n2023年7月10日\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：郑州金水河灾后重建 防洪标准 投资规模\n\n网页标题：投资超25亿元 金水河综合整治工程预计2024年底完工\n\n网页链接：http://henan.people.com.cn/n2/2022/0217/c351638-35137575.html\n\n发布时间：2022-02-17T08:33:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：投资超25亿元 金水河综合整治工程预计2024年底完工\n2022年02月17日08:33 | 来源：大河网-顶端新闻·河南商报\n2月10日，金水河沿河路正在拓宽施工顶端新闻·河南商报记者 刘鸿翔/摄\n与郑州相伴上千年的金水河，首要功能就是泄洪。不过在历史上，它也曾10年6次发生严重水灾。因此，郑州人对它的治理，始终没有停止脚步。\n近日，它又迎来新一轮的治理规划。据悉，此次综合整治后，金水河防洪标准，有望提升至100年一遇。\n历史上的金水河经常发生水灾\n金水河算不上大江大河，可上千年来，它对郑州的作用举重若轻。\n近日，这条“明星”河流迎来好消息，郑州市发改委批复金水河综合整治工程初步设计，将对郭家咀水库至东风渠段金水河进行治理，涉及河道总长约22.3公里，概算投资25.3亿元。\n郑州市城乡建设局回应称，金水河综合整治工程是河南省灾后恢复重建的标志性项目之一，将以保障行洪安全为核心打通河道阻水点，增加河道行洪排涝能力，做好雨污水分流，保障行洪安全。工程计划于2023年12月主体完工（涉铁段外），2024年底全部完工。\n顶端新闻·河南商报记者查阅资料发现，历史上郑州金水河曾多次发生严重水灾。\n1953年，金水河14处决口，郑州市内积水成灾；1956年，金水河燕庄桥附近决口，造成飞机场被淹；1958年，金水河泛滥，国棉四厂、五厂进水，造成停产。\n郑州市城区河道管理处相关负责人吴振江介绍，上世纪90年代，郑州市对金水河进行了一次大规模综合整治，此后金水河很长时间里基本上没有发生过严重水灾，直到2021年。\n也正是因为频发水灾，金水河河道在人为干预下，曾进行过大规模改道。\n“现在的中原路，有很长一段就是金水河原来的河道。”吴振江介绍，金水河进入郑州主城区后，流至中原路一带时，原本会转向东，然后到二七路附近，再向北流至金水路南侧。\n上世纪30年代，民国政府对金水河进行改道，形成了金水河目前的河道。\n郑州人对金水河的治理一直持续至今\n从大禹治水到挖通大运河再到南水北调，从古至今，坚信“人定胜天”的中国人，有着丰富的治水经验。金水河畔的郑州人，也不断对这条河流进行整治。\n据《郑州市金水河志》记载，新中国成立后，金水河迎来大规模治理，主要分为治水阶段、治河阶段以及综合整治阶段。\n从1949年到1958年，金水河6次发生较大水灾，郑州市政府以治水为核心，10年里11次组织人力疏挖河道，提升排洪能力。\n在治河阶段，郑州市曾对大石桥至中和路桥一带的河道进行疏通，使金水河抗洪标准提高到接近10年一遇。\n金水河的全方位蜕变，始于1997年，在这一年，郑州市投入1.5亿元资金，开展了大规模综合整治。\n“治理前的金水河，两岸大部分地方都是土堤。”吴振江回忆，那个时候两岸堤坝杂草丛生，各种树木野蛮生长，“跟小时候乡下的护村堤差不多。”\n“遇到洪水，土堤肯定容易决口。”吴振江介绍，在1997年的综合整治中，金水河城区段河道、堤坝都进行了硬化处理，降低了淤泥堆积的可能性，也降低了决口风险，防洪能力大大提升。\n当时，政府在金水河设置了10多个橡胶坝，既可以调节河水流量，起到一定防汛作用，又可以形成“小瀑布”景观，供市民欣赏。\n综合整治后的金水河，变身名副其实的景观河，成了郑州一张名片。\n在郑州大学老校区一带，还有人看准商机，提供租赁船只...\n对于郑州市来说，尽管金水河首要功能是泄洪，但这并不意味着，对它的治理，只需要考虑防汛。\n吴振江表示，从上世纪七八十年代开始，金水河还曾面临水源枯竭难题。金水河迫切需要再次进行综合整治\n从天然河流到郑州主要泄洪通道，金水河有着天然优势。在郑州主城区内，金水河落差达20多米，洪水可以自行流走，无需人工抽取。\n不过同样因为是天然河流，也让金水河河道宽度参差不齐，在流量较大时，容易形成阻水点。\n随着时代发展，目前的金水河及沿岸配套设施已经无法满足实际需要，再次进行综合整治迫在眉睫。\n“20多年过去了，很多设施已经跟不上了。”吴振江表示，1997年综合整治时为金水河配备的基础设施，经过风吹雨打，很多已经到了该“退休”的年纪，“一些建筑小品损坏严重，各种线缆、管道错综复杂，有的铁质设备锈迹斑斑。”\n以金水河沿线桥梁为例，顶端新闻·河南商报记者了解到，其中有不少始建于上世纪五六十年代。例如人民路桥始建于1952年，燕庄桥始建于1955年，建设路桥始建于1965年。\n尽管一些桥梁曾经进行过加固、翻新，但总体而言，对它们进行功能、质量提升，十分有必要。\n另外据郑州市城区河道管理处统计，在去年水灾过程中，金水河从南三环与西三环交叉口到中州大道段，共计出现大大小小的损毁111处。虽然目前均已进行了修复，但难免会留下一些“疤痕”，这也在一定程度上加剧了金水河综合整治的迫切性。\n金水河防洪标准将提升至100年一遇\n金水河综合整治势在必行，未来，这条河流将走向何方？\n顶端新闻·河南商报记者从郑州市城乡建设局获悉，金水河综合整治工程对恢复金水河河道功能、保障行洪安全、提高城市应急管理能力十分重要，“工程范围为目前河道两岸绿地范围以内，局部拓展至现状河道两岸小区围墙或市政道路边线。”\n郑州市城乡建设局回应称，金水河综合整治工程结合上游郭家咀水库重建及南截流沟建设，提升金水河防洪标准至100年一遇。\n未来，郑州金水河将成为贯穿南北、串联周边，具备多元复合功能的都市绿脉，将补齐水安全、水资源、水环境、水生态短板，确保行洪安全，保障河道基础功能。\n\n\n========\n搜索关键词：世界银行汶川地震重建项目 评估报告 经济影响\n\n网页标题：【外资司支持世界银行开展汶川地震灾后恢复重建项目评估】-国家发展和改革委员会\n\n网页链接：https://www.ndrc.gov.cn/fzggw/jgsj/wzs/sjjdt/201908/t20190826_1037000_ext.html\n\n发布时间：2019-08-26T17:21:17+08:00\n\n网页内容：外资司支持世界银行开展汶川地震灾后恢复重建项目评估\n8月23日下午，外资司应约接受世界银行独立评价局项目绩效评估报告任务组组长stephenhutton一行评估访谈，向世行介绍了汶川地震灾后恢复重建基本情况，对世行贷款汶川地震灾后恢复重建项目进行评价并提出建议。\n外资司介绍，在党中央国务院的领导下，我有力有序地组织开展了抗震救灾工作，通过各地政府对口支援、社会各界捐赠参与、震区人民积极建设，用两年时间提前完成汶川地震灾后恢复重建主要任务。在恢复重建过程中，国际社会和国际金融组织通过援助和优惠贷款等多种形式，发挥了积极重要作用。\n外资司认为，世行不仅为灾区恢复重建提供资金帮助，还在项目设计、建设规范、建设质量、运营维护和能力建设等多方面提供支持，通过提升防灾减灾能力实现社会效益、经济效益与环境效益的和谐统一。鉴于救灾本身的应急属性，外资司建议世行研究简化救灾项目的贷款审批流程，使世行在全球有关地区灾情发生后第一时间发挥其应有作用。\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：世界银行汶川地震重建项目 评估报告 经济影响\n\n网页标题：China: Building Back Stronger\n\n网页链接：https://www.worldbank.org/en/results/2018/05/11/building-back-better-plus\n\n发布时间：2018-05-11T00:00:00+08:00\n\n网页内容：At the request of the government, the Bank quickly prepared an emergency loan to support the restoration and enhancement of basic infrastructure, health and education services in the provinces of Sichuan and Gansu. The project aimed to reduce the vulnerability to seismic and flood hazards and build the capacity of local governments to manage the recovery program and infrastructure.\nThe project took a “Build Back Better Plus” approach that ensured that all project construction activities used higher seismic-proof standards and flood risk management codes, while ensuring a balance between reconstruction activities and laying a foundation for the longer-term sustainable economic recovery and development of the project towns. For the first time in China, a flexible framework approach was used which allowed the provinces to identify and prepare subprojects efficiently.\n12.7 million\nThe Wenchuan Earthquake Recovery Project restored and improved critical infrastructure, health, and education services in severely affected counties in China’s Sichuan and Gansu provinces, directly benefiting about 12.7 million people.\nResults\nThe project was implemented in 27 severely affected counties in Sichuan and Gansu between 2009 and 2014, and restored...\nWater. Ten water supply plants were built with 230 km of water supply pipelines and four pumping stations, improving access to households and commercial and industrial users, as well as for urban fire-fighting purposes. This led to an increase of 25% in coverage of households and commercial buildings with a continuous 24-hour water supply compared to the pre-earthquake situation.\nWastewater. Nine wastewater treatment plants were rehabilitated or constructed, and 102.5 km of sewerage pipelines and 492.5 km of storm water drainage pipelines were built. As a result, the sewage treatment ratio in the project counties increased by over 50% compared to the pre-earthquake situation.\nSolid waste collection and disposal (Sichuan only). Investments under this project led to an average increase of 42% in the collection and disposal ratio of solid waste garbage compared to the pre-earthquake situation.\nHealth. 67 health facilities were built, equipped and are fully operational. The number of hospital beds in the project counties increased by 67% and 35% in Sichuan and Gansu respectively. The new facilities has greatly enhanced diagnostic and treatment capacities and provide a wider range of in-patient and out-patient medical services, resulting in higher admissions than before the earthquake.Education (Gansu Only). Seven new schools were built and equipped with text books, computer equipment and laboratories, classroom, canteen and dormitory furniture, and sporting equipment. Training courses were provided for 450 principals, teachers and administrators, and covered a broad range of education topics, including new emergency management procedures.\nCapacity building. The provincial, municipal and county level governments of both provinces benefited from a broad range of training and capacity building activities related to the World Bank’s safeguards, financial management and procurement, as well as technical areas such as investigation, design and contract supervision, with a total of 3,701 training days completed.\nEconomic growth. Compared with pre-earthquake level, GDP grew between 117% and 198%, primarily driven by growth in the non-agricultural sectors. Secondary industries (including both industrial and construction sectors) increased between 116% and 286% and service sectors grew by 135% and 201%. Per capita income across the board increased between 90% and 154% in project counties.\nBank Group Contribution\nA US$710 million Emergency Loan was provided by the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (IBRD) to support recovery investments in Sichuan (US$510 million) and Gansu (US$200 million), focusing on the reconstruction of infrastructure such as roads, bridges, water supply, wastewater, solid waste, and health facilities in selected counties in both provinces, and also on the reconstruction of education facilities in Gansu.\nThe Bank mobilized US$1.5 million grant from the Global Facility for Disaster Reduction and Recovery (GFDRR) to support the preparation of policy notes, the involvement of international experts, and the training of teachers and school staff, as well as hospital staff. The GFDRR grant also supported the government to review and evaluate the implementation of the national reconstruction materplan and six sector-specific reconstruction plans.\nThe Bank also mobilized a Global Environment Facility (GEF) grant of US$1 million to support assessment of potential chemical contamination from industries affected by the earthquake.\nThe International Finance Corporation (IFC), the private sector arm of the World Bank Group, created credit lines for small and medium-sized businesses in the aftermath of the earthquake.\nPartners\nIn addition to GFDRR and GEF, the French Development Agency (AfD) provided a grant to support early engagement of French consultants who worked with the World Bank team to develop selection criteria and appraise subprojects, and help build early capacity of provincial project management offices. Finally, a GEF grant supported the assessment of the chemical contamination in the immediate aftermath of the earthquake.\nMoving Forward\nThe project supported the training of post-disaster recovery teams in the Asia-Pacific region, strengthened the part­nership with the government of China on disaster risk management activities, and disseminate China’s experience and expertise in disaster preparedness and relief to other countries in the region and worldwide. A report on the lessons learned from the reconstruction has been published for international dissemination and many of the lessons from the Wenchuan Earthquake reconstruction are being applied elsewhere.\nThe Lushan Earthquake struck Sichuan in 2013, almost five years after the Wenchuan Earthquake, and affected 2.2 million people. The World Bank-supported Lushan Earthquake Reconstruction and Risk Reduction Project has learned and incorporated lessons from the Wenchuan Earthquake Recovery Project.\nTo this day, the Wenchuan Earthquake serves an important reminder to other countries prone to earthquakes of the importance of measures ensuring construction quality and structural resilience of buildings and infrastructure. Moreover, the recovery process, its efficacy, and speed in Sichuan, serves an example of the large-scale reconstruction that aims not only to replace the lost and damaged assets but also to bring the reconstructed and new infrastructure to a higher quality standards, based on the upgraded building codes and regulations, and use the reconstruction to improve local economies and living standards of the affected population.\nBeneficiaries\nPan Li, Deputy County Mayor of Yanting: “Through implementation of the World Bank-supported project, our city’s environment has greatly improved, we have an expanding urban space and flourishing businesses and tourism. Compared to 2008, our GDP has increased by 127%, and urban per capita income by 180%. We have gained significant ecological, social and economic benefits. This is welcomed and appreciated by the people.”\nZhang Yufang, Resident of Cangxi: “The change is enormous. In the past, we had only dirt roads and lived in mud houses. Today where we live, what we eat, wear and use is all different.”\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：世界银行汶川地震重建项目 评估报告 经济影响\n\n网页标题：Wenchuan Earthquake Recovery (P114107)\n\n网页链接：http://documents.worldbank.org/curated/en/104521468242672224/pdf/ISR-Disclosable-P114107-06-13-2016-1465827607155.pdf\n\n网页内容：The World Bank Wenchuan Earthquake Recovery (P114107)\nPublic Disclosure Authorized Public Disclosure Authorized No\nPublic Disclosure Copy\nImplementation Status \\u0026 Results Report\nWenchuan Earthquake Recovery (P114107)\nEAST ASIA AND PACIFIC | China | Social, Urban, Rural and Resilience Global Practice Global Practice | IBRD/IDA | Emergency Recovery Loan | FY 2009 | Seq No: 10 | ARCHIVED on 29-May-2016 | ISR23214 |\nImplementing Agencies: Gansu Provincial PMO, Sichuan Provincial Construction Commission\nKey Dates\nKey Project Dates\nBank Approval Date:12-Feb-2009\nPlanned Mid Term Review Date:14-May-2012\nOriginal Closing Date:30-Jun-2014\nEffectiveness Date:17-Jun-2009 Actual Mid-Term Review Date:28-May-2012 Revised Closing Date:31-May-2016\nProject Development Objectives\nProject Development Objective (from Project Appraisal Document)\nTo restore essential infrastructure, health, and education services to at least levels existing prior to the Wenchuan Earthquake, and where appropriate, to provide for expansion of services, while reducing the vulnerability to seismic and flood hazards and building capacity of local governments to manage the recovery program.\n2.4 Project Support Gansu:(Cost $4.00 M)\nOverall Ratings\nName\nPrevious Rating\n6/13/2016\nPublic Disclosure Copy\nCurrent Rating\nPage 1 of 12\nPublic Disclosure Copy\nThe World Bank Wenchuan Earthquake Recovery (P114107)\nImplementation Status \\u0026 Results Report\nProgress towards achievement of PDO\nOverall Implementation Progress (IP)\nOverall Risk Rating\nModerately Satisfactory\nIn Sichuan Province, restoration of essential infrastructure is largely satisfactory with 100% of water supply services completed and 95% of the roads have been completed, with only one road extending beyond loan closing. The health facilities have been 100% restored and are fully operational. The project financed health and water facilities are operating at levels higher than before the earthquake. The vulnerability to flood and seismic hazard of all project financed infrastructure has been reduced through much improved seismic engineering standards and relocating facilities to less vulnerable sites. The 2013 Lushan Earthquake affected project areas, but the infrastructure and facilities financed by the project withstood the earthquake and little damage was reported compared to other infrastructure in the region. The health and infrastructure agencies at the county level benefitted from training to reduce vulnerability to natural hazards and improve operation and maintenance practices.\nIn Gansu Province, restoration of essential water infrastructure has reached 90% of the expected total. The Moba Gorge Dam will be completed after loan closing by August 2016, and only than the Cheng County water supply treatment plant can be connected to the reservoir and become operations. There have been some changes in the location and alignment of urban roads in Cheng County and Wudu City since not all resettlement issues could be resolved. Almost all project financed schools, hospitals, water and wastewater treatment plants in Gansu are now operational. However there is one school in Wan County that still needs to be connected to the water supply system financed by the County to become fully operational. The client should now prepare the final Borrower's completion report and assist the Bank with data collection and analysis for delivery of the final completion report in late November 2016. Much higher seismic standards were applied to project financed infrastructure and investments, less vulnerable sites were selected and in some cases specific infrastructure was financed to reduce exposure to flood risks. The capacity of health, education and infrastructure agencies was strengthened in the planning and implementation of infrastructure projects and reduce vulnerability to natural disasters.\n6/13/2016\nPublic Disclosure Copy\nPage 2 of 12\nPublic Disclosure Copy\nThe World Bank\nImplementation Status \\u0026 Results Report\nWenchuan Earthquake Recovery (P114107)\n6/13/2016\nAll hospitals are fully operational, and the Cheng County Hospital was expanded is now also functioning normally.\nGansu - Percentage of reconstruction (a) primary and (b) secondary schools that reach enrollment rates of (a) 99% and (b) 80% respectively (Percentage, Custom)\nBaseline Actual (Previous) Actual (Current) End Target\nValue 0.00 85.00 100.00 100.00\nDate 12-May-2008 28-Oct-2015 20-May-2016 31-May-2016\nComments\nThe Number 3 School in Wan County is still lacking access to...\nComments\nMost of the benefits were related to the improvements in the water, sewage and drainage networks along roads in 15 Counties and Districts in Sichuan Province and 6 Counties in Longnan Municipality in Gansu Province. In addition, water treatment plants, wastewater treatment plants and/or pumping stations were built in 6 Counties in Sichuan and 3 Counties in Gansu.\nOverall Comments\nData on Financial Performance\nDisbursements (by loan)\nProject Loan/Credit/TF Status Currency Original Revised Cancelled Disbursed Undisbursed Disbursed\nP114107 IBRD-76160 Effective USD 710.00 710.00 0.00 690.30 19.70 97%\nKey Dates (by loan)\nProject Loan/Credit/TF Status Approval Date Signing Date Effectiveness Date Orig. Closing Date Rev. Closing Date\nP114107 IBRD-76160 Effective 12-Feb-2009 20-Mar-2009 17-Jun-2009 30-Jun-2014 31-May-2016\nCumulative Disbursements\n6/13/2016\nPublic Disclosure Copy\nPage 11 of 12\nPublic Disclosure Copy\nThe World Bank\nImplementation Status \\u0026 Results Report\nWenchuan Earthquake Recovery (P114107)\n640\nAmi\n480\n320\n160\n0\n2009 Q3 2010 Q3 2011 Q3 2012 Q3 2013 Q3 2014 Q3 2015 Q3 2016 Q3 2016 Q4\nOriginal Amount Formally Revised Amount Actual Amount\nRestructuring History\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：世界银行汶川地震重建项目 评估报告 经济影响\n\n网页标题：Quake's influence on GDP limited -- china.org.cn\n\n网页链接：http://www.china.org.cn/business/news/2008-06/23/content_15871443_2.htm\n\n网页内容：Quake's influence on GDP limited\nIn infrastructure, more than 12 million buildings were damaged in the earthquake-affected areas. The damaged power transmission lines added up to 1,978 kilometers. Nearly 2,300 dams, including two large ones and 28 medium ones, were damaged. The quake has wrecked 22,000 kilometers of road and tunnels, affecting 21 expressways, 15 interprovincial highways and 2,756 rural roads.\nBut both the SIC and the World Bank agree that the earthquake, while enormous in human tragedy, won't have a great impact on the wider economy.\n\"The quake won't change the fundamentals of China's economy and reconstruction work will outweigh the short-term disruption to production. Instead, it may give economic growth a small boost,\" said the SIC.\nAccording to its study, the 13 counties and cities ravaged by the earthquake in Sichuan Province contributed a total of 0.34 percent to the nation's gross domestic product and the direct losses from the earthquake may trim the gross domestic product by 0.1 percentage point.\nBut the new demand created by the recovery work is expected to boost the investment ratio by 1.25 percentage points. Together with a boost to consumption, it may lift the nation's GDP by 0.4 percentage point and help power economic growth by a net 0.3 percentage point.\nThe World Bank also said the quake is expected to have only a moderate impact on China's economy.\n\"Although the damage to the affected areas is huge, the affected areas account for only a small part of China's economy,\" it said. \"In the face of this kind of natural disaster, China is fortunate to have a large and diverse economy that can continue to function well and that can finance quick reconstruction in the affected areas.\"\nThe central and local governments plan to allocate about 170 billion yuan annually through 2010 to fund rebuilding work in the earthquake-hit areas while domestic and foreign donations have reached about 43.7 billion yuan.\nThe World Bank, however, viewed the relief and reconstruction funding as additional fuel which will boost demand in the economy.\nIt has also revised the forecast for China's economic growth in 2008 to 9.8 percent from 9.4 percent in a previous report in April.\n\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：世界银行汶川地震重建项目 评估报告 经济影响\n\n网页标题：Wenchuan Earthquake Recovery\n\n网页链接：https://projects.worldbank.org/en/projects-operations/project-detail/P114107\n\n网页内容：Repayments include payments made by borrowers, debt relief provided by IDA, and payments made by third parties on behalf of the borrowers. The disbursed amount less the repaid amount, for loans and credits, may not equal the loan or credit balance outstanding due to exchange rate movements.\nRatings\nIMPLEMENTATION RATINGS\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003cth\u003eName\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eReview\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth\u003eDate\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eCounterpart Funding\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eModerately Satisfactory\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e2016-05-29\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eFinancial Management\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eModerately Satisfactory\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e2016-05-29\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eMonitoring and Evaluation\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eModerately Unsatisfactory\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e2016-05-29\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eOverall Implementation Progress (IP)\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eModerately Satisfactory\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e2016-05-29\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\u003ctd\u003eProcurement\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003eModerately Satisfactory\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e2016-05-29\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\